        "question": "My grand daughter who is just under 2 years old had caps put on her front teeth on March 20th of this year and now her gums are infected. She had the procedure in the office. They took her to the dentist today and were told to brush her teeth better and to rub mouth wash on the gum area. Her gums bleed after brushing and they are saying it is a good thing... as I recall, gums bleeding is usually a bad thing. since things change from year to year with research, I wanted to clarify this situation.",
